From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO weekly shield report

Tapping the shield card of the new tab page (now with a "Weekly
report" link) opens the weekly shield report, with the mascot:

- the ads and trackers blocked this week,
- how it compares with the same days of last week (Monday to
  yesterday, so a half-finished today never skews it), and last
  week's total,
- a bar for each day from Monday to Sunday, today in the CromIKO
  accent color,
- the 5 sites where CromIKO blocked the most,
- the 5 trackers and ad servers blocked the most (the eyeo ad blocker
  tells which addresses it blocked; Cromite's filter only counts),
- early in the week, while this week is still empty, last week's
  lists,
- a link to the ad blocker settings.

cromiko_shield_stats.cc now also keeps the counts of the last 14 days,
of the sites and of the trackers of the week, and the top 10 sites and
trackers of last week. The lists keep the 300 largest when they pass
400 entries. Incognito tabs are still not counted, and nothing leaves
the device. Since the sites are a form of history, deleting browsing
history (also with the Fire button) removes them, for the deleted
sites; the counts stay.

